+# Formal-methods Workplan & Artifact Packaging (Aegis)
+
+Purpose
+- Provide a clear workplan to produce formal-methods artifacts, run model↔code proofs, and produce an auditor-ready package with reproducible runs.
+
+Scope & Goals
+- Identify high-risk controllers (canary controller, retrain trigger, approval engine, cosign promotion) and produce machine-checkable invariants.
+- Run model checking (Apalache/TLA+), TLC exploration and SMT/back-end checks (Z3) where applicable.
+- Collect all artifacts (specs, checks, logs, source mappings, signed manifests) into a signed audit bundle for reviewers.
+
+Steps
+1. Inventory & scoping
+   - List control loops and map to TLA+ actions (use docs/formal/proof_mapping.md).
+   - Prioritize controllers by risk: canary_promote, retrain_trigger, approvals service, cosign signer.
+
+2. Author invariants & lemmas
+   - Write safety invariants that capture desired properties (no silent promotion of high-risk actions; rollback on excessive error rate; evidence present before promote).
+   - Add liveness/integrity properties as needed.
+
+3. Run model checking
+   - Use Apalache/TLC and Z3 (as configured) and capture logs.
+   - Iterate until counterexamples are addressed or invariants refined.
+
+4. Produce reproducible artifact
+   - Use ops/formal/run_formal_pipeline.sh to run checks and produce a gzipped bundle with signed manifests.
+   - Store bundle in a secure S3 bucket and Rekor-register the top-level bundle manifest.
+
+5. Deliver to auditors
+   - Package artifacts with Docker runner (ops/formal/Dockerfile) so auditors can reproduce the checks locally.
+
+Deliverables
+- TLA+ specs, Apalache/TLC logs, Z3/SMT outputs
+- Signed manifest file for the auditor bundle (cosign + Rekor)
+- Checklist completed (ops/formal/audit_checklist.md)
+
