+# Cosign / KMS Operational Playbook (Aegis)
+
+Purpose
+- Operationalize KMS-backed cosign signing across CI, ensure secure key lifecycle, and prepare audit artifacts for cryptographic review.
+
+High-level flow
+1. Provision KMS/HSM key in your cloud (AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault).
+2. Restrict IAM policies to allow signing only from CI or designated operator principals.
+3. Store COSIGN_KMS_URI in Vault and as CI secret (org-level).
+4. Update CI to require COSIGN_KMS_URI for production model signing.
+5. Rotate keys using a staged rollout: create new key -> switch CI -> smoke sign -> revoke old key.
+6. Collect usage logs and Rekor entries for audit and hand them to auditors.
+
+Operator checklist
+- Create key with asymmetric signing usage (RSA/ECC depending on provider).
+- Ensure key has proper key policy/audit logging enabled.
+- Place COSIGN_KMS_URI into Vault under secret aegis/cosign_kms.
+- Update GH Actions org secrets with COSIGN_KMS_URI (staged).
+- Run ops/security/cosign_kms_setup.sh to verify signing from CI runner.
+- Run ops/security/collect_kms_audit.sh and package logs for auditors.
+
