+# Auto-Approval Policy Plan
+
+Goal
+- Permit safe automatic execution of low-risk actions when sufficient signed evidence is present; continue requiring human approval for high-risk actions.
+
+Design
+- Policy engine (OPA) hosts rego rules (ops/policy/rego/auto_approve.rego).
+- Evaluate before run: provide input {action, evidence} where evidence contains manifest presence and cosign=true/false.
+- If OPA returns allow=true, run proceeds automatically and an evidence manifest is recorded for the action execution.
+- If OPA returns allow=false and action is high-risk, route to approvals service for human signoff (ops/approvals).
+
+Implementation steps
+1. Deploy OPA as a sidecar or central policy server and load auto_approve.rego.
+2. Integrate ops/policy/opa_client.py in high_risk.require_human_approval path: allow auto-approve if OPA policy permits.
+3. Ensure evidence payload includes cosign verification (CI) or proof of signing.
+4. Record evidence for both auto-approvals and human approvals.
+5. Audit: ensure auto-approved actions are visible in autonomy dashboard and require periodic human review.
+
+Security considerations
+- Only accept auto-approval if evidence is cryptographically verifiable (cosign KMS + Rekor).
+- Define strict whitelist of action names that may be auto-approved via rego rules.
+
